{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1373341-shapeshifitng-horror-of-hulk","id":1373341,"title":"Shapeshifitng Horror of Hulk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-07T01:22:41-08:00","id":1373341,"title":"Shapeshifitng Horror of Hulk","content":"The new comicbook Hulk series - <i>Immortal Hulk</i> - has some very good inspiration for <b>Werewolf</b>. Gruesome shapechanging, each night forced transformations. Sounds a bit like Harmony 10 character, like one from <i>American Werewolf in London</i>. Maybe some good ideas can be mined from it? Or you have other inspirations in <i>Hulk</i> franchise?<br /> <br /> Below video summing up <i>Immortal Hulk</i> run till this day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2G7Dqzwajqg\" data-code=\"2G7Dqzwajqg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2G7Dqzwajqg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-27-2020, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T11:02:52-08:00","id":1373406,"title":"","content":"There's some good ideas in it, though a running theme is him being sort of unique in his destructive capability and consistently at god-tier, which doesn't really fit with a werewolf in a pack. He has teammates but you would have to really overestimate their roles to even call them sidekicks, as they're more like the extended pack members, just with powers. That said it's a good comic, telling the Hulk as a more horror-leaning story.<br /> <br /> Joss Whedon actually <a href=\"https://www.ign.com/articles/2015/04/23/joss-whedon-on-why-a-planet-hulk-movie-might-not-work\" target=\"_blank\">made a point of calling out the parallel of Hulk with a werewolf</a> a while back, mentioning that a Hulk story is more a werewolf story than a classic superhero story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}